  "guideAppTitle": "Using the app",
  "@guideAppTitle": {
    "description": "The guide's first heading, under the Talmud's words that open it: how the app helps with the practice."
  },
  "guideAppBody": "Today shows this week’s parsha and today’s reading. The rings fill as you read: Mikrah, Mikrah again, then Targum.\nRead from a printed Chumash? Tap “I read it in a Chumash”. After Shabbat, log what you read on Shabbat.\nMissed a day? Read it with the next day’s reading and it’s made up; if not, a grace day covers it.\nPress and hold a verse to bookmark it, add a note, copy, share or ask about it.\nListen reads the text aloud for you to follow — an aid, not a substitute for reading.",
  "@guideAppBody": {
    "description": "Under the guide's Using the app heading: one point to a line, each shown after a bullet. It quotes readFromBook, and names Today, Listen and grace days as the app does."
  },
