  "searchSpellingFallback": "No verse has “{query}”. Showing “{variant}”, as the Torah spells it.",
  "@searchSpellingFallback": {
    "description": "Above the results of a search in Hebrew that no verse holds as typed, when the same words with fewer ו and י, as the Torah often spells them (אהרן for אהרון, כהן for כוהן), were found instead. query is what the reader typed; variant is the Torah's spelling whose verses are shown.",
    "placeholders": {
      "query": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "variant": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "sourcesSunDescription": "Worked out on the device with the formulas of the NOAA Solar Calculator (after Meeus, Astronomical Algorithms), and checked against Hebcal, whose times are the default: candles lit 18 minutes before sunset, 20 in Israel, 40 in Jerusalem and 30 in Haifa and Zikhron Ya’akov, and Shabbat ending when the sun is 8.5° below the horizon. In Settings, under Reading & customs, candles can be lit at other minutes, and Shabbat can end 42, 50 or 72 minutes after sunset, as a local luach has them.",
  "@sourcesSunDescription": {
    "description": "On the Texts & sources page, under Sunrise and sunset: how Shabbat times are worked out, their defaults, and the choices Settings offers."
  },
  "communityComingSoon": "The community is coming soon. Until then, your reading stays on this device; to move it, use a backup, in Settings under Your data.",
  "@communityComingSoon": {
    "description": "In a build without the community (COMMUNITY=off): one calm line in About, under the title page, and in the guide, after Using the app. Your data is the Settings page with the backup file (settingsData)."
  },
  "guideAppBodyNoCommunity": "Today shows this week’s parsha and today’s reading. The rings fill as you read: Mikrah, Mikrah again, then Targum.\nRead from a printed Chumash? Tap “I read it in a Chumash”. After Shabbat, log what you read on Shabbat.\nMissed a day? Read it with the next day’s reading and it’s made up; if not, a grace day covers it.\nPress and hold a verse to bookmark it, add a note, copy or share it.\nListen reads the text aloud for you to follow — an aid, not a substitute for reading.",
  "@guideAppBodyNoCommunity": {
    "description": "guideAppBody in a build without the community (COMMUNITY=off), where a verse can't be asked about: the same points, kept in step with it, but the fourth, which leaves out asking."
  },
